stateDiagram-v2

%% This diagram models one HeartbeatTransaction owned by one Replica.
%% The transaction handles many heartbeat periods, but only for one
%% coordinator term. It ends when control passes to ElectionTransaction.

%% [*] used as a source means "the transaction lifecycle begins".
%% STOPPED means the object exists, but no heartbeat timer is active yet.
[*] --> STOPPED

%% When the transaction starts, the owning Replica chooses its role by
%% comparing its own ID with the current coordinator ID.
STOPPED --> COORDINATOR: start as coordinator
STOPPED --> WATCHING: start as follower

%% HeartbeatTick is an internal message. The Akka Scheduler sends it to the
%% coordinator Replica's own mailbox. Handling the tick broadcasts a network
%% HEARTBEAT and schedules the next one-shot HeartbeatTick.
COORDINATOR --> COORDINATOR: HeartbeatTick

%% A follower starts a watchdog when it enters WATCHING. A valid HEARTBEAT is
%% one sent by the coordinator monitored by this transaction. It cancels and
%% replaces the current watchdog, while the transaction remains in WATCHING.
WATCHING --> WATCHING: valid HEARTBEAT

%% WatchdogExpired is also an internal scheduler message. "current" means its
%% coordinator ID and generation match the active watchdog. Older cancelled
%% watchdog messages are stale and must be ignored by the Java implementation.
WATCHING --> ELECTION_REQUESTED: current WatchdogExpired

%% ELECTION_REQUESTED prevents multiple election requests for the same
%% coordinator failure. Once ElectionTransaction starts, this heartbeat
%% transaction has completed. A new coordinator term gets a new instance.
%% [*] used as a destination means "the transaction lifecycle ends".
ELECTION_REQUESTED --> [*]: ElectionTransaction started
